---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Install ArkheionX"
  description="Install ArkheionX from public source, inspect the installer, update, uninstall, and understand what the installer does."
>
  <main class="install-page">
    <section class="install-hero">
      <div class="install-hero__copy">
        <p class="install-kicker">Install</p>
        <h1>Install ArkheionX from source.</h1>
        <p>
          The current public distribution path is a source install from GitHub main. Binary releases
          are not published yet. The installer creates a local checkout, Python virtual environment,
          and command wrappers on your machine.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="install-status">
        <div>
          <span>Channel</span>
          <strong>source install</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Branch</span>
          <strong>main</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Binary release</span>
          <strong>not published</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Review mode</span>
          <strong>local-first</strong>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section install-section--primary">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Fast path</p>
        <h2>Install with one command.</h2>
        <p>
          Use this after you are comfortable with the installer behavior. For a more cautious path,
          inspect the script first.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="install-command-stack">
        <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Recommended for first use</p>
        <h2>Inspect first, then run.</h2>
        <p>
          This path downloads the installer, lets you read it locally, and only runs it after you
          explicitly approve.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="install-command-stack">
        <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install.sh -o arkheionx-install.sh
less arkheionx-install.sh
bash arkheionx-install.sh</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Manual path</p>
        <h2>Install directly from GitHub.</h2>
        <p>
          This is the transparent source path. It is useful for local development, auditability,
          or when you want to control every step yourself.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="install-command-stack">
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Yudis-bit/arkheionx.git
cd arkheionx
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel
python -m pip install -e .
arkheionx version</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section install-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Repository identity</p>
        <h2>Use the ArkheionX name publicly.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="install-list-card">
        <p>
          The public repository has been renamed to <code>Yudis-bit/arkheionx</code>.
          New users should use the canonical GitHub URL. ArkheionX is review
          infrastructure, not an exploit dump.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section install-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Requirements</p>
        <h2>What you need.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="install-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Operating system</h3>
          <p>Linux or macOS for the installer path.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Python</h3>
          <p>Python 3.11 or newer.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Git</h3>
          <p>Used to clone or update the public source checkout.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Network</h3>
          <p>Needed for GitHub clone and Python package installation.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section install-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Installer behavior</p>
        <h2>What the installer does.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="install-list-card">
        <ul>
          <li>Checks for Linux or macOS.</li>
          <li>Checks for Git and Python 3.11 or newer.</li>
          <li>Clones or updates the public GitHub repository.</li>
          <li>Creates a managed virtual environment under <code>~/.arkheionx</code>.</li>
          <li>Installs ArkheionX in editable source mode.</li>
          <li>Creates command wrappers under <code>~/.local/bin</code>.</li>
          <li>Runs <code>arkheionx version</code> as a basic installation check.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section install-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Safety boundary</p>
        <h2>What the installer does not do.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="install-list-card install-list-card--warning">
        <ul>
          <li>It does not ask for private keys, seed phrases, or secrets.</li>
          <li>It does not call RPC endpoints by default.</li>
          <li>It does not run live-chain transactions.</li>
          <li>It does not run Foundry or exploit tests during installation.</li>
          <li>It does not confirm vulnerabilities or produce audit conclusions.</li>
          <li>It does not submit reports or automate bounty workflows.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Update</p>
        <h2>Update an existing source install.</h2>
        <p>
          Re-running the installer should update the managed checkout and refresh the local
          environment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="install-command-stack">
        <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install.sh | bash
arkheionx version</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Uninstall</p>
        <h2>Remove the local install.</h2>
        <p>
          This removes the managed ArkheionX directory and command wrappers created by the installer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="install-command-stack">
        <pre><code>rm -rf "$HOME/.arkheionx"
rm -f "$HOME/.local/bin/arkheionx" "$HOME/.local/bin/arkup"</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-section install-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="install-kicker">Troubleshooting</p>
        <h2>Common install issues.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="install-troubleshooting">
        <details>
          <summary><span>Command not found after install</span></summary>
          <p>
            Add <code>$HOME/.local/bin</code> to your shell PATH, then restart your terminal.
          </p>
          <pre><code>export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"</code></pre>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary><span>Python version is too old</span></summary>
          <p>
            Install Python 3.11 or newer, then rerun the installer.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary><span>Git is missing</span></summary>
          <p>
            Install Git with your system package manager, then rerun the installer.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary><span>Clean reinstall</span></summary>
          <p>
            Remove the managed directory and wrappers, then run the installer again.
          </p>
          <pre><code>rm -rf "$HOME/.arkheionx"
rm -f "$HOME/.local/bin/arkheionx" "$HOME/.local/bin/arkup"
curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-boundary">
      <p class="install-kicker">Current limitation</p>
      <h2>Installer promotion waits on final package validation.</h2>
      <p>
        The website can document the install path now, but public promotion should wait until a fresh
        source install confirms <code>arkheionx version</code>, <code>arkheionx doctor</code>, release
        readiness, and the full validation suite.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
